    "details": "<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>CODE VOYAGE</strong> is a pirate-themed technical challenge testing logic, pseudocode, technical knowledge, and strategy across two rounds. Teams navigate a grid-based problem and battle through a high-stakes technical bidding round, where every decision shapes their final score.</p>\n<p><em><strong>Navigate the Code. Master the Challenge. Claim the Voyage.</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Details:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Date:</strong> 18th October 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> 10:30 AM</li>\n<li><strong>Venue:</strong> Guru Tegh Bahadur Institute of Technology</li>\n<li><strong>No. of Rounds:</strong> 2</li>\n<li><strong>Pre-requisites:</strong> 1 working laptop or phone per team.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to all students.</li>\n<li>Inter-college participants allowed.</li>\n<li>Team Size: 2&ndash;4 members per team.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Flow:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Grid Navigation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams solve a grid-based logical challenge by determining the correct path or sequence of instructions. Solutions must be submitted in pseudocode.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Pirate Bidding Battle</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams receive 10 coins (50 points each) and bid for technical questions. The highest bidder gets 60 seconds to answer. Correct answers earn 2&times; the bid, while incorrect answers lose the bid.</li>\n<li>Bids must be placed in multiples of 50 points and cannot exceed the team&rsquo;s available balance. Once placed, a bid cannot be withdrawn.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Regulations:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial round must be solved using pseudocode; executable code is not required. Only one device per team is permitted in Round 1.</li>\n<li>Use of AI is not permitted during either round.</li>\n<li>Follow team size (2-4 members).</li>\n</ul>",
    "end_date": "2026-10-17T19:30:00+05:30",
